{
  "_comment": [
    "The tempo each bar is meant at, where the page changes it, and the contract",
    "both implementations must keep: `score_schema.tempo_in_force` in the",
    "backend, which the analysis judges each bar against, and",
    "`lib/score/tempoMap.ts` in the app, which Listen plays and the bar editor",
    "starts a new tempo from. Two walks in two languages; this file is how they",
    "stay one rule, as `start_at.json` does for trimming.",
    "",
    "`stated` is per bar, from bar 1: null is the piece's opening tempo, a",
    "number a `new_tempo`'s stated BPM. Each marking pushes the tempo it leaves,",
    "`a tempo` pops one, and \"Tempo I\" goes back to the opening.",
    "`tempo_changes` rows are [measure, kind, text, bpm]."
